# The child modules must carry their net-declaration initialisers, so nothing
# in the hierarchy is left undriven.  Without the fix `leaf`'s t1/t2/t3 have no
# driver and every output below the top reads X -- yet the netlist still
# "matches" formally in the sense that both sides are X, so `check -assert` is
# the gate that actually fails.
read_uhdm slpp_all/surelog.uhdm
hierarchy -check -top dut
proc
flatten
opt_clean
check -assert
